# .vercelignore uses gitignore syntax, where '#' only starts a comment at the
# START of a line. A trailing comment after a pattern becomes part of the
# pattern and silently matches nothing — which is exactly how research/ and
# archive/ ended up publicly served on the first deploy. Keep comments on
# their own lines.

# Internal. Must never be published. Note BOTH spellings: the v1 site lives in
# .archive/ (dotted), and a bare `archive` pattern does not match it.
archive
.archive
research
.impeccable
.DS_Store
.env.local

# Research captures, not referenced by any page.
assets/shots

# Source. The site is pre-built, so the generator is not needed at the edge.
# home.js and articles.js belong here for the same reason build.js does — they
# are the generator's input, and without a rule they upload as static files and
# are fetchable at /home.js. design/ holds the mockup references.
build.js
products.js
home.js
articles.js
README.md
design

# The transform and build scripts, likewise. Without this they are uploaded as
# static files and become publicly fetchable — /tools/chat.test.js and friends.
# NOTE the exception that must NOT be added here: api/. That directory is the
# serverless function plus the knowledge base it requires, and excluding it
# would take the assistant offline.
tools

# Agent/tool scratch captures. Gitignored, but .vercelignore's existence means
# .gitignore is not consulted at deploy time, so they must be listed here too.
.playwright-mcp
old-inquiry.png
# a 15-byte stray from some earlier redirect test, in the tree but not the site
-w

# Added with the clean-URL migration. Same rule as build.js above: these are
# the generator's inputs and its paperwork, not files the edge should serve.
# site.config.json in particular is fetchable at /site.config.json without one.
package.json
site.config.json
scripts
DOMAIN-CUTOVER.md
